    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "f3305b0f25eccb88cedc3d231b66125b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"photongluon-currents-and-crossing\">Photon\u2013gluon currents and crossing</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/photon_radiation.py\">Real QCD radiation</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/quark_gluon_scattering.py\">Quark\u2013gluon scattering</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate both diagrams for each process:\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\gamma^*g\\to q\\bar q||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(q\\gamma^*\\to gq||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(q\\bar q\\to\\gamma^*g||)</marimo-tex>. Keep the quark mass, photon virtuality and\ngeneric SU(<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N_c||)</marimo-tex>) color. Model particles and vertices are selected by name.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">These calculations reproduce FeynCalc's\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/GaGl-QQbar\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">photon\u2013gluon fusion</a>,\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/QGa-GlQ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">QCD Compton</a>, and\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QCD/Tree/QQbar-GaGl\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">annihilation</a>\nexamples. Each channel is generated independently before checking crossing.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The off-shell photon current is contracted with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-g_{\\mu\\nu}||)</marimo-tex> without\na photon spin average, matching the references. Incoming quark/gluon\nspins and colors are averaged. This current contraction is not a physical\nvirtual-photon cross section; a lepton tensor is needed for an observable\ninvolving a virtual photon.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
